module DASHI.Physics.YangMills.BalabanYM4SharpenedLiteralRowA1PositiveBetaExact where

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ROW A1 (LEMMA 1), STEPS 6 AND 7:  THE SHARPENED LITERAL STATEMENT,
--   END TO END, AND ITS WELD INTO THE SOURCE TRAJECTORY COMPILER.
--
-- PRIMARY SOURCE
--
-- Tadeusz Bałaban, "Renormalization Group Approach to Lattice Gauge Field
-- Theories. I. ...", Communications in Mathematical Physics 109 (1987),
-- 249--301.  DOI: 10.1007/BF01215223.  Locators: Euclidean covariance
-- (5.6),(5.7); beta extraction (5.36)--(5.42); end of Sect. 5 for the
-- dependence of beta_j on all preceding effective couplings.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS.
--
-- `BalabanYM4LiteralWilsonFPHaarPositiveBetaExact.LiteralRowA1` assembles
--
--     beta_j = (11/24) C_A + R_j + sum_{d<n} Delta_{d,j}
--            >= (11/24) C_A - 15 * cellMeasure * epsilon - C gamma / 2 > 0
--
-- from two hypotheses that are both stronger than the argument needs:
--
--   (i) a SEPARATE lower bound -epsilon on each of the four orbit densities,
--       which discards the (4,6,4,1) cancellation and pays the factor 15;
--  (ii) per-shell influence increments dominated by the SPECIFIC profile
--       2^-(d+2), which forces a one-step RG contraction factor kappa <= 1/2.
--
-- `BalabanYM4CancellationPreservingFourOrbitGateExact` removes (i) and
-- `BalabanYM4GeneralSummableHistoryBudgetPositiveBetaExact` removes (ii).
-- This module runs the whole Row A1 chain on the two weakened hypotheses at
-- once, so the literal statement now reads
--
--     beta_j = (11/24) C_A + R_j + sum_{d<n} Delta_{d,j}
--            >= b_-(G) = (11/24) C_A - cellMeasure * epsilon - K gamma * B
--            >  0 ,        1 + kappa * B = B ,   any kappa in [0,1) ,
--
-- uniformly in the shell index j, the length n of the preceding
-- small-coupling history, the volume and the cutoff, with the group entering
-- only through C_A(G) > 0; and it is welded to the source-normalized coupling
-- recurrence, giving linear growth of the inverse coupling towards the
-- ultraviolet at rate b_-(G).
--
-- WHAT IS STILL OPEN.  Exactly the same two physical leaves as before, in
-- their weakened form, and nothing here supplies either:
--
--   (A) the literal momentum-space joint Wilson + reduced Faddeev-Popov +
--       Haar density of the CMP109 background-field vacuum polarisation,
--       together with a bound on the negative part of its (4,6,4,1)-weighted
--       COMBINATION, uniform in cutoff, volume and scale;
--   (B) SOME cutoff- and volume-uniform one-step contraction factor
--       kappa < 1 for the literal Balaban RG map, plus Lipschitz dependence
--       of the literal shell coefficient on the effective-coupling state.
--
-- Exact rational arithmetic; no postulate, no hole, no receipt, no pragma.
-- Checked with `agda --safe`.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

